      "heading": "B — Audience, level and prerequisites: the point system",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, level and prerequisites: the point system\nAudience: first-time Missouri Class F applicants, from teens on an instruction permit to adult newcomers, who will start building a driving record once licensed.\nWhy it matters to a first-timer: point values and the advisory, suspension and revocation thresholds are exact test items [A01], and the point reduction steps and failure to appear rules are easy to mix up [A02].\nLevel: threshold and duration recall with several look-alike number pairs; moderate load.\nPrerequisites: the alcohol and drugs chapter for intoxication-related reinstatement, and the license chapters on suspension and revocation.\n",
